-- title:
--   The function space $\mathscr{C}ont_k(X,Y)$ into a compactly generated weakly Hausdorff space $Y$ is weakly Hausdorff
-- statement:
--   Function spaces with values in a compactly generated weakly Hausdorff space are weakly Hausdorff.
--
--   A topological space is *compactly generated* if its topology is determined by the continuous maps into it from compact Hausdorff spaces (no separation axiom), and *weakly Hausdorff* if the image of every continuous map from a compact Hausdorff space is closed. For compactly generated spaces $X,Y$ the *compactly generated function space* is
--   $$\mathscr{C}ont_k(X,Y):=k\big(\mathrm{C}(X,Y)\big),$$
--   the set $\mathrm{C}(X,Y)$ of continuous maps $X\to Y$ with the $k$-ification of the compact-open topology having as sub-base the sets $N(g,K,U)=\{f:(f\circ g)(K)\subseteq U\}$, where $K$ is a compact Hausdorff space, $g:K\to X$ is continuous and $U\subseteq Y$ is open. (The $k$-ification of a topology is the finest topology with the same continuous maps from compact Hausdorff spaces.)
--
--   **Statement.** Let $X$ and $Y$ be compactly generated topological spaces and assume that $Y$ is weakly Hausdorff. Then $\mathscr{C}ont_k(X,Y)$ is weakly Hausdorff.
--
--   Since $\mathscr{C}ont_k(X,Y)$ is compactly generated by construction, it is an object of the category $\mathbf{CGWH}$ of compactly generated weakly Hausdorff spaces. As $\mathscr{C}ont_k$ is the internal hom of the cartesian closed category of compactly generated spaces, this shows that the full subcategory $\mathbf{CGWH}$ is closed under exponentials and therefore inherits the cartesian closed structure. No separation condition on the source $X$ is needed.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** `CGSpace.ContK X Y` is the type synonym of `C(X, Y)` from the platform definition file `CGSpace_FunctionSpace`, carrying the $k$-ification of the compact-open topology defined by test maps; `CGWH.WeaklyHausdorffSpace` is from the definition file `CGWH_WeakHausdorff`. All spaces live in one universe `u`; `CompactlyGeneratedSpace` is Mathlib's notion (test spaces `CompHaus.{u}`, no separation axiom). The hypotheses that $X$ and $Y$ are compactly generated are kept as in the source.
-- source:
--   A. M. Masullo, The Music of the Primes, draft of 20 November 2026, https://math216.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/the-music-of-the-primes.pdf, p. 854, Proposition E.2.2.10 (first assertion); classical reference (as cited by the paper at this place): N. Strickland, The category of CGWH spaces (available online), Prop. 2.24

import Definitions.Def_CGWH_WeakHausdorff
import Definitions.Def_CGSpace_FunctionSpace

open Topology TopologicalSpace

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

namespace CGWH

theorem weaklyHausdorffSpace_contK
    (X Y : Type u) [TopologicalSpace X] [TopologicalSpace Y]
    [CompactlyGeneratedSpace X] [CompactlyGeneratedSpace Y] [WeaklyHausdorffSpace Y] :
    WeaklyHausdorffSpace (CGSpace.ContK X Y) := by sorry

end CGWH
